Files kept byte-identical to upstream, at their original paths:

  src/linked-list.js
  src/linebreak.js
  src/formatter.js
  lib/hypher.js
  lib/en-us.js
  lib/jquery-1.4.2.js      (used only by the upstream examples/, unchanged)
  examples/                (upstream demo pages, unchanged)
  LICENSE                  (upstream text, unchanged)

`git log -- src/linebreak.js` therefore still shows only upstream commits.
The sha256 of every vendored file is recorded in
`engine/_upstream.generated.mjs` and re-verified by `test/upstream.test.mjs`.

New work, licensed under the BSD 2-Clause License as well:

  engine/chars.mjs         CJK character classification and advance widths
  engine/nodes.mjs         box/glue/penalty model for CJK (the core addition)
  engine/index.mjs         public layout API
  engine/metrics.mjs       quality metrics
  engine/greedy.mjs        greedy baseline used for comparison
  engine/_upstream.generated.mjs   generated ESM wrapper (do not edit)
  bin/hanline.mjs          CLI
  demo/                    browser demo
  test/                    test suite
  scripts/                 build, verification and benchmark harnesses
  README.md, NOTICE        this notice

No upstream source file was modified. The CJK capability does not exist
upstream in any form: `grep -rniE "cjk|chinese|japanese|korean|kinsoku" src/ lib/`
returns nothing at the forked commit, and `src/formatter.js` splits on /\S+/,
so a Chinese paragraph becomes a single indivisible box.
